{"id": "EUVD-2026-71788", "enisaUuid": "c0e8d4d5-2169-3155-9fad-7390f0d2d876", "description": "Unidata netcdf-c through 4.10.1 contains an out-of-bounds write vulnerability in NC4_HDF5_inq_attname() that copies HDF5 attribute names into a fixed 256-byte buffer without length validation. Attackers can craft HDF5 files with oversized attribute names to overflow the destination buffer, causing memory corruption and crashes when applications enumerate attribute names.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T22:38:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-08T17:45:51", "baseScore": 8.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/Unidata/netcdf-c", "https://github.com/Unidata/netcdf-c/blob/v4.10.1/libhdf5/hdf5attr.c", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/unidata-netcdf-c-through-4.10.1-out-of-bounds-write-via-oversized-hdf5-attribute-name"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-86095", "GHSA-mm3m-jp7w-cj3m"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a18b78cc-acdc-3844-a88f-c0cd2cae6b13", "product": {"name": "NetCDF-C", "vendor": {"name": "NSF Unidata"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22644.10.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ac7c7f97-dc6e-3e58-a017-1fbfda75dc6b", "vendor": {"name": "Unidata"}}], "isExploited": false}